0 247 539 [
[(increment with [mod 1e+06] to)]
[(make a note tag \050acts like a)]
[(MIDI pitch to identify the)]
[(note to [poly]\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 20 373 [
[(Here we take the previous patch and make it polyphonic, with)]
[(8 voices. The single voice which we had before has been made)]
[(into an abstraction, [sampvoice], which we instantiate in 8)]
[(copies with the [clone] object. Earlier we used sends and)]
[(receives to pass messages to "cutoff", etc, but here if we)]
[(did that the copies of [sampvoice] would be sending messages)]
[(to each other, so we combine the control and the audio)]
[(computation in the [sampvoice] abstraction without using send)]
[(and receive. Click on [clone] one to see how.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 20 147 [
[(There's some bother because [poly] expects to track note on)]
[(and note off messages separately as they would come from a)]
[(MIDI keyboard. So we assign each note a unique fake "pitch",)]
[(use [makenote] to generate the note-off messages, and run)]
[([poly] on the resulting stream. We then discard both pitch)]
[(and velocity for the note offs with [stripnoe] \050using the)]
[(velocity only to strip note-offs\051 and rebuild the original)]
[(message adding the voice number we just scored.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
